§289g local TP2 (log-convexity) of the Weil KERNEL at fine scale h: minor det[[W(x,y),W(x,y+h)],[W(x+h,y),W(x+h,y+h)]]>=0?
  h=3.0: 144 minors, 0 negative, worst = 4.615e-12 -> TP2 holds
  h=2.0: 144 minors, 0 negative, worst = 1.883e-12 -> TP2 holds
  h=1.0: 144 minors, 0 negative, worst = 4.481e-13 -> TP2 holds
DONE. TP2 at fine h => Weil kernel is log-convex at the continuous level => strong support the kernel is TP2 (RH route).
any negative => TP2 breaks at fine scale => the empirical matrix-TP was a coarse-sampling artifact; lead weakens.
